# Frontend Modular Monolith

## Purpose

Admin UI (`web/`) is a **modular monolith in the browser**: one SPA build (`web/dist`), domain folders as compile-time modules. Same invariants as Go `cmd/control` (`modular-monolith.mdc`, `structure.mdc`):

- Thin composition root (`pages/`)
- Domain-owned UI (`ui/<domain>/`)
- No ceremony trees (`dto/`, `usecase/`, `providers/`)
- Cold path first: server owns filter/sort/aggregate (`ui.mdc`, `cold-path.mdc`)

**Quality reference:** `lead-intent-processor` — `internal/crm/{admin,store,webhook}` owns CRM surface; `internal/app` (~18 prod `.go`) wires only. Admin SPA mirrors that split: `pages/` = wire, `ui/<domain>/` = product.

Cross-ref: `ui.mdc` (layout, grid, milestones), `react.mdc` (render hot path), `boundaries.mdc` (coupling limits), `naming.mdc`.

